Kintsugi built-in modernization content

This directory is derived from the "code-modernization" plugin in
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official (plugins/code-modernization),
at commit c8874f5ad883e26428f483ffa4d537cc81489e64.
Copyright Anthropic. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE.

Changes from the upstream content:

- Deleted: upstream assets and presentation templates; Claude Code plugin metadata; host hook registration and APIs; terminal pane, review deck, X-ray and other host UI; telemetry; and tests/fixtures used only by the plugin host or pane.
- Added: the server-side JobOutput Python hook and specification, including credential scanning, artifact-shape validation, redacted JSON findings, bounded/fail-closed input handling, and Python tests; Kintsugi reader-layout helpers and Vitest coverage; the Kintsugi `understand` command (understand.md) and its scripts (units_from_topology.py, merge_traceability.py, write_work_items.py) with Python tests, which have no upstream counterpart.
- Adapted: agent, command, workflow, script, hook-reader, and documentation content to Kintsugi's split between runtime jobs, member harnesses, and the portal; workspace artifact paths and commit boundaries; and the package's test/lint/typecheck setup. The reader functions remain pure and are intended for future portal progress presentation.

The complete Kintsugi adaptation history is recorded in the repository. No Claude Code plugin or plugin marketplace is shipped.

Build and review

The member command `build` and the runtime stage `review` of the `modernize` plugin (ADR-0071) are written for Kintsugi; they have
no upstream counterpart, but their method was read from, and credits, these Apache License 2.0 plugins of
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official: code-modernization (commands/modernize-transform.md and
modernize-verify.md; agents/test-engineer.md and architecture-critic.md: tests that name the rule they pin, a suite that executed
no case proves nothing, the canary, a reviewer who did not write the code), feature-dev (agents/code-architect.md and
code-reviewer.md: read, plan, build, then review by someone else) and pr-review-toolkit (agents/pr-test-analyzer.md,
silent-failure-hunter.md, code-reviewer.md: reviewers that each look for one kind of fault). No text was copied; the skills
`build-method`, `unit-testing` and `code-review` and the agent `code-reviewer` are Kintsugi's own words.

Mermaid diagrams skill

skills/mermaid-diagrams is the mermaid skill of WH-2099
(https://github.com/WH-2099/mermaid-skill, .claude/skills/mermaid) at commit
982d903, as published: SKILL.md and references/. Copyright 2026 WH-2099.
Licensed under the MIT License; see skills/mermaid-diagrams/LICENSE. Change:
the name in the SKILL.md frontmatter is mermaid-diagrams instead of mermaid.
The references derive from the Mermaid documentation (https://mermaid.js.org/,
MIT). scripts/mermaid_lint.py is Kintsugi's own standard-library validator.

Some of the syntax-safety rules checked by scripts/mermaid_lint.py (keywords as
ids, ids starting with o or x, comments on their own line, linking nodes rather
than subgraphs) were informed by the ideas of awesome-skills/mermaid-syntax-skill
(https://github.com/awesome-skills/mermaid-syntax-skill, commit
933d1a6bc6b438f01aeb8811c6a0f16ab4d5c505); they are written in Kintsugi's own
words and no text was copied.
